[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_script")
entry_name = "Lua Pattern Matching"
description = "Lua uses string.match with patterns (not regex) to find substrings.

Common pattern classes:
%d  digits, %a  letters, %s  whitespace, %w  alphanumeric

print(string.match(\"abc123\", \"%d+\"))  -- 123
print(string.match(\"Hello World\", \"%a+\"))  -- Hello

The + modifier means one or more. You can capture groups:

local _, num = string.match(\"id:42\", \"(%a+):(%d+)\")
print(num)  -- 42

Lua patterns are simpler than regex but sufficient for most string parsing."
keyword = "string.match"
language = "lua"
category = "Medium"
